1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,637
Part five. Then the market voted.

2
00:00:02,206 --> 00:00:03,437
On November 19th,

3
00:00:03,483 --> 00:00:06,594
Anthropic listed at $83 a share.

4
00:00:06,954 --> 00:00:09,706
It opened around $111 and closed its first

5
00:00:09,741 --> 00:00:11,308
day near $97.

6
00:00:11,738 --> 00:00:14,733
By Friday, it had slipped to about $87,

7
00:00:14,756 --> 00:00:16,312
still above its listing price,

8
00:00:16,672 --> 00:00:18,274
as tech stocks fell around it.

9
00:00:18,704 --> 00:00:20,445
The deal raised more than $80 billion,

10
00:00:20,527 --> 00:00:23,522
and up to $93 billion if the underwriters

11
00:00:23,557 --> 00:00:24,776
take their extra shares.

12
00:00:25,263 --> 00:00:27,504
So far, neither man is proven right.

13
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:28,503
On the show,

14
00:00:28,549 --> 00:00:30,987
both sides agreed the first day says little.

15
00:00:31,347 --> 00:00:33,065
The real test is time.

16
00:00:33,379 --> 00:00:35,341
Which brings us back to the one number

17
00:00:35,434 --> 00:00:37,338
both of them agree will decide it.
